{
  "title": "54: al-Qamar القمر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاِقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ وَانْشَقَّ الْقَمَرُ‏(1)\nAEQTARABATE SAA-A’TO WAANSHAQQA AL-QAMARU.\nThe Hour (of Judgment) is nigh, and the moon is cleft asunder. \nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا اٰيَةً يُّعْرِضُوْا وَيَقُوْلُوْا سِحْرٌ مُّسْتَمِرٌّ‏(2)\nWA YYARAWA AAYATAL YYUA’REZOOA WAYAQOOLOOA SEHRUM MMUSTAMERRUN.\nBut if they see a Sign, they turn away, and say, “This is (but) transient magic.” \nوَكَذَّبُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ وَكُلُّ اَمْرٍ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‏(3)\nWA KAZZABOO WAT TABA-O’O AHWAAA-AHUM WA KULLO AMRIN MMUSTAQERRUN.\nThey reject (the warning) and follow their (own) lusts but every matter has its appointed time. \nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَنْۢبَآءِ مَا فِيْهِ مُزْدَجَرٌۙ‏(4)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MENAL AL-AANBAAE MAA FEEHE MUZDAJARUN.\nThere have already come to them Recitals wherein there is (enough) to check (them), \nحِكْمَةٌۢ بَالِغَةٌ‌ فَمَا تُغْنِ النُّذُرُۙ‏(5)\nHEKMATUN BAALEGHATUN FAMAA TUGHNE AN-NUZURU.\nMature wisdom;- but (the preaching of) Warners profits them not. \nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ‌ۘ يَوْمَ يَدْعُ الدَّاعِ اِلٰى شَىْءٍ نُّكُرٍۙ‏(6)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM YAWMA YADU’U DAA-E’ ELAA SHAY-IN NNUKURIN.\nTherefore, (O Prophet,) turn away from them. The Day that the Caller will call (them) to a terrible affair, \nخُشَّعًا اَبْصَارُهُمْ يَخْرُجُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ كَاَنَّهُمْ جَرَادٌ مُّنْتَشِرٌۙ‏(7)\nKHUSSHAA’AN AABSAARUHUM YAKHROJOONA MENAL AJDAASE KA-ANNAHUM JARAADUN MMUNTASHERUN.\nThey will come forth, their eyes humbled - from (their) graves, (torpid) like locusts scattered abroad, \nمُّهْطِعِيْنَ اِلَى الدَّاعِ‌ؕ يَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَسِرٌ‏(8)\nMMUHTEE’EENA ELAL AD-DAAE’E YAQOOLO KAAFEROON HAAZAA YAWMUL A’ASERUN.\nHastening, with eyes transfixed, towards the Caller!- “Hard is this Day!”, the Unbelievers will say. \nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ فَكَذَّبُوْا عَبْدَنَا وَقَالُوْا مَجْنُوْنٌ وَّازْدُجِرَ‏(9)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN FA KAZZABOO A’ABDANAA WA QAALOO MAJNOONUN WWAAZDUJERA.\nBefore them the People of Noah rejected (their messenger): they rejected Our servant, and said, “Here is one possessed!”, and he was driven out. \nفَدَعَا رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَغْلُوْبٌ فَانْتَصِرْ‏(10)\nFA-DA-A’A WAL AANNEAA MAGHLOOBUN FAANTASER.\nThen he called on his Lord: “I am one overcome: do Thou then help (me)!” \nفَفَتَحْنَاۤ اَبْوَابَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَآءٍ مُّنْهَمِرٍ ۖ‏(11)\nFAFATAHNAA ABWAABAS SAMAAA-E BEMAAA-IM MUNHAMER.\nSo We opened the gates of heaven, with water pouring forth. \nوَّفَجَّرْنَا الْاَرْضَ عُيُوْنًا فَالْتَقَى الْمَآءُ عَلٰٓى اَمْرٍ قَدْ قُدِرَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nWA FAJJARNAL ARZA O’YOONAN FALTAQAL MAAA-O A’LAA AMRIN QAD QODER.\nAnd We caused the earth to gush forth with springs, so the waters met (and rose) to the extent decreed. \nوَحَمَلْنٰهُ عَلٰى ذَاتِ اَلْوَاحٍ وَّدُسُرٍۙ‏(13)\nWAHAMALNAAHU A’LAA ZAATIL AALWAAHIN WWADUSURIN.\nBut We bore him on an (Ark) made of broad planks and caulked with palm-fibre: \nتَجْرِىْ بِاَعْيُنِنَا‌ۚ جَزَآءً لِّمَنْ كَانَ كُفِرَ‏(14)\nTAJREE BEAAA’YUNENAA JA-ZAAA-AWN LEMAN KAANA KUFERA.\nShe floats under our eyes (and care): a recompense to one who had been rejected (with scorn)! \nوَلَقَدْ تَّرَكْنٰهَاۤ اٰيَةً فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(15)\nWA LAQAD TTARAKNAAHAA AAYATAL FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd We have left this as a Sign (for all time): then is there any that will receive admonition? \nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(16)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nBut how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning? \nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd We have indeed made the Qur'an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition? \nكَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(18)\nKAZZABAT A’ADUN FA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nThe 'Ad (people) (too) rejected (Truth): then how terrible was My Penalty and My Warning? \nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيْحًا صَرْصَرًا فِىْ يَوْمِ نَحْسٍ مُّسْتَمِرٍّۙ‏(19)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM REEHAN SARSARAN FEE YAWMIL NAHSIN MMUSTAMERRIN.\nFor We sent against them a furious wind, on a Day of violent Disaster, \nتَنْزِعُ النَّاسَۙ كَاَنَّهُمْ اَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُّنْقَعِرٍ‏(20)\nTANZEU’U NAASA KA-ANNAHUM AAA’JAAZU NAKHLIN MMUNQAE’ERIN.\nPlucking out men as if they were roots of palm-trees torn up (from the ground). \nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(21)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nYea, how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning! \nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(22)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nBut We have indeed made the Qur'an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition? \nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(23)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO BEALNNUZURE.\nThe Thamud (also) rejected (their) Warners. \nفَقَالُوْۤا اَبَشَرًا مِّنَّا وَاحِدًا نَّتَّبِعُهٗۤۙ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‏(24)\nFA-QAALOO AABASHARAN MINNAA WAAHEDAN NNATTABEU’UH INNAA EZAL LAFEE ZALAALIM WWASUU’URIN.\nFor they said: “What! a man! a Solitary one from among ourselves! shall we follow such a one? Truly should we then be straying in mind, and mad! \nءَاُلْقِىَ الذِّكْرُ عَلَيْهِ مِنْۢ بَيْنِنَا بَلْ هُوَ كَذَّابٌ اَشِرٌ‏(25)\nAALQEAAA AZ-ZEKRU A’LAYHE MIN BAYNENAA BAL HOWA KAZZAABUN AASHERUN.\n“Is it that the Message is sent to him, of all people amongst us? Nay, he is a liar, an insolent one!” \nسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ غَدًا مَّنِ الْكَذَّابُ الْاَشِرُ‏(26)\nSA-YA’LAMOONA GHADAN MMANE AL-KAZZAABU AL-AASHERU.\nAh! they will know on the morrow, which is the liar, the insolent one! \nاِنَّا مُرْسِلُوا النَّاقَةِ فِتْنَةً لَّهُمْ فَارْتَقِبْهُمْ وَاصْطَبِرْ‏(27)\nINNAA MURSELOOA AN-NAAQATE FETNATAN LAHUM FAARTAQEBHUM WAASTABER.\nFor We will send the she-camel by way of trial for them. So watch them, (O Salih), and possess thyself in patience! \nوَنَبِّئْهُمْ اَنَّ الْمَآءَ قِسْمَةٌۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ۚ كُلُّ شِرْبٍ مُّحْتَضَرٌ‏(28)\nWANABBEHUM ANNAL MAAA-AH QESMATUN BAYNAHUM KULLO SHERBIN MMUHTAZARUN.\nAnd tell them that the water is to be divided between them: Each one's right to drink being brought forward (by suitable turns). \nفَنَادَوْا صَاحِبَهُمْ فَتَعَاطٰى فَعَقَرَ‏(29)\nFANAADAWA SAAHEBAHUM FATAA’AATAA FAA’AQARA.\nBut they called to their companion, and he took a sword in hand, and hamstrung (her). \nفَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(30)\nFA-KAYFA KAANA A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nAh! how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning! \nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً فَكَانُوْا كَهَشِيْمِ الْمُحْتَظِرِ‏(31)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM SAYHATANW WAAHEDATAN FA KAANOO KAHASHEEME AL-MUHTAZERE.\nFor We sent against them a single Mighty Blast, and they became like the dry stubble used by one who pens cattle. \nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(32)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd We have indeed made the Qur'an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition? \nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ ۢ بِالنُّذُرِ‏(33)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO LOOTIM BEALNNUZURE.\nThe people of Lut rejected (his) warning. \nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حَاصِبًا اِلَّاۤ اٰلَ لُوْطٍ‌ؕ نَّجَّيْنٰهُمْ بِسَحَرٍۙ‏(34)\nINNAA ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM HAASEBAN ILLAA AALA LOOTIN NNAJJAYNAAHUM BESAHARIN.\nWe sent against them a violent Tornado with showers of stones, (which destroyed them), except Lut's household: them We delivered by early Dawn, \nنِّعْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ مَنْ شَكَرَ‏(35)\nNNEA’MATAN MIN I’NDENAA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA MAN SHAKARA.\nAs a Grace from Us: thus do We reward those who give thanks. \nوَلَقَدْ اَنْذَرَهُمْ بَطْشَتَنَا فَتَمَارَوْا بِالنُّذُرِ‏(36)\nWA LAQAD AANZARAHUM BATSHATANAA FATAMAARAWA BEALNNUZURE.\nAnd (Lut) did warn them of Our Punishment, but they disputed about the Warning. \nوَلَقَدْ رَاوَدُوْهُ عَنْ ضَيْفِهٖ فَطَمَسْنَاۤ اَعْيُنَهُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(37)\nWA LAQAD RAAWADOOHU A’N ZAYFEH FATAMASNAA AAA’YUNAHUM FA-ZOOQOO A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\nAnd they even sought to snatch away his guests from him, but We blinded their eyes. (They heard:) “Now taste ye My Wrath and My Warning.” \nوَلَقَدْ صَبَّحَهُمْ بُكْرَةً عَذَابٌ مُّسْتَقِرٌّ‌ ۚ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD SABBAHAHUM BUKRATANW A’ZAABUN MMUSTAQERRUN.\nEarly on the morrow an abiding Punishment seized them: \nفَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابِىْ وَنُذُرِ‏(39)\nFA-ZOOQOO A’AZAABEAA WANUZURE.\n“So taste ye My Wrath and My Warning.” \nوَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْاٰنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(40)\nWA LAQAD YASSARNAA QURAANA LELZZEKRE FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd We have indeed made the Qur'an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition? \nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ النُّذُرُ‌ۚ‏(41)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-A AALA FIR-A’WNA AN-NUZURU.\nTo the People of Pharaoh, too, aforetime, came Warners (from Allah). \nكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كُلِّهَا فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ اَخْذَ عَزِيْزٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(42)\nKAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA KULLEHAA FAAKHAZNAAHUM AAKHZA A’AZEEZIN MMUQTADERIN.\nThe (people) rejected all Our Signs; but We seized them with such Penalty (as comes) from One Exalted in Power, able to carry out His Will. \nاَكُفَّارُكُمْ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ اُولٰٓئِكُمْ اَمْ لَكُمْ بَرَآءَةٌ فِى الزُّبُرِ‌ۚ‏(43)\nAAKUFFAARUKUM KHAYRUL MIN AOOLAAAEKUM AM LAKUM BARAAATUN FIL AZ-ZUBURE.\nAre your Unbelievers, (O Quraish), better than they? Or have ye an immunity in the Sacred Books? \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ نَحْنُ جَمِيْعٌ مُّنْتَصِرٌ‏(44)\nAM YAQOOLOONA NAHNO JAMEE-U’L MMUNTASERUN.\nOr do they say: “We acting together can defend ourselves”? \nسَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّوْنَ الدُّبُرَ‏(45)\nSAYUHZAMU AL-JAMU’U WA YOWALLOONAL AD-DUBURA.\nSoon will their multitude be put to flight, and they will show their backs. \nبَلِ السَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ اَدْهٰى وَاَمَرُّ‏(46)\nBALIL SAA-A’TO MAWE’EDUHUM WA SAA-A’TO AADHAA WAAMARRU.\nNay, the Hour (of Judgment) is the time promised them (for their full recompense): And that Hour will be most grievous and most bitter. \nاِنَّ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ وَّسُعُرٍ‌ۘ‏(47)\nINNAL MUJREMEEN FEE ZALAALIM WWASUU’URIN.\nTruly those in sin are the ones straying in mind, and mad. \nيَوْمَ يُسْحَبُوْنَ فِى النَّارِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْؕ ذُوْقُوْا مَسَّ سَقَرَ‏(48)\nYAWMA YUSHABOONA FIL NAAR A’LAA WUJOOHEHEM ZOOQOO MASSAN SAQARA.\nThe Day they will be dragged through the Fire on their faces, (they will hear:) “Taste ye the touch of Hell!” \nاِنَّا كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنٰهُ بِقَدَرٍ‏(49)\nINNAA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALAQNAAHO BEQADARIN.\nVerily, all things have We created in proportion and measure. \nوَمَاۤ اَمْرُنَاۤ اِلَّا وَاحِدَةٌ كَلَمْحٍۢ بِالْبَصَرِ‏(50)\nWA MAA AAMRUNAA ILLAA WAAHEDATUN KALAMHIN BIL-BASARE.\nAnd Our Command is but a single (Act), like the twinkling of an eye. \nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَاۤ اَشْيَاعَكُمْ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُّدَّكِرٍ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD AHLAKNAL AASHYAAA’AKUM FA HAL MIN MMUDDAKERIN.\nAnd (oft) in the past, have We destroyed gangs like unto you: then is there any that will receive admonition? \nوَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ فَعَلُوْهُ فِى الزُّبُرِ‏(52)\nWA KULLO SHAY-IN FAA’ALOOHU FIL AZ-ZUBURE.\nAll that they do is noted in (their) Books (of Deeds): \nوَ كُلُّ صَغِيْرٍ وَّكَبِيْرٍ مُّسْتَطَرٌ‏(53)\nWA KULLO SAGHEERIN WWAKABEERIN MMUSTATARUN.\nEvery matter, small and great, is on record. \nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَهَرٍۙ‏(54)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WWANAHARIN.\nAs to the Righteous, they will be in the midst of Gardens and Rivers, \nفِىْ مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيْكٍ مُّقْتَدِرٍ‏(55)\nFEE MAQA’ADE SEDQIN I’NDAL MALEEKIN MMUQTADERIN.\nIn an Assembly of Truth, in the Presence of a Sovereign Omnipotent. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qamar (The Moon)\nThis ’Makki’ Surah has 55 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the fact of the person who recites this Surah will shine like the full moon on the Day of Reckoning. The best time to recite this Surah is at night and this carries the highest reward.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that the one who recites this Surah will have a mount from Jannah on which he will sit when he wakes from his grave. Whoever keeps this Surah under his cap or turban at the time of Friday prayers will be highly respected by the people and his difficulties will be eased."
}
